in/articleshow/132830463.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-03T19:28:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Natasha Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132834290,imgsize-2820918.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ancient Egyptians mummified thousands of crocodiles at Kom Ombo. Modern DNA has finally revealed where the sacred reptiles came from]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132829667.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/ancient-egyptians-mummified-thousands-of-crocodiles-at-kom-ombo-modern-dna-has-finally-revealed-where-the-sacred-reptiles-came-from/articleshow/132829667.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/ancient-egyptians-mummified-thousands-of-crocodiles-at-kom-ombo-modern-dna-has-finally-revealed-where-the-sacred-reptiles-came-from/articleshow/132829667.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-03T16:52:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132829760,imgsize-1427434.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2016, nations created the world's largest marine reserve in Antarctica]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132825146.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Ross Sea Marine Protected Area became a global conservation milestone after years of negotiation.  This vast Antarctic reserve was established by the CCAMLR member states in 2016.  It protects a significant marine ecosystem supporting diverse wildlife and vital phytoplankton blooms.  Scientific study of climate change impacts is also a key benefit of this protected area.  However, limitations exist regarding fishing and the reserve's 35-year lifespan.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-2016-countries-came-together-to-protect-a-huge-part-of-antarcticas-ocean-creating-the-worlds-largest-marine-reserve/articleshow/132825146.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-2016-countries-came-together-to-protect-a-huge-part-of-antarcticas-ocean-creating-the-worlds-largest-marine-reserve/articleshow/132825146.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-03T13:48:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132825169,imgsize-162122.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Houston student Aiden Jo, 14, and his origami-inspired answer reached a national science final]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132833463.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Aiden Jo, a bright fourteen-year-old, has ingeniously crafted a collapsible container called 'Squeeze-gami' aimed at minimizing waste volume. His innovative solution has earned him a spot among ten national finalists vying for a prestigious top prize along with mentorship from renowned 3M scientists. This competition emphasizes STEM-oriented solutions to tackle everyday challenges and environmental concerns, with winners set to be revealed following live challenges in October 2026.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/houston-student-aiden-jo-14-saw-bulky-packaging-as-a-design-problem-his-origami-inspired-answer-reached-a-national-science-final/articleshow/132833463.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/houston-student-aiden-jo-14-saw-bulky-packaging-as-a-design-problem-his-origami-inspired-answer-reached-a-national-science-final/articleshow/132833463.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-03T19:26:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132833463,imgsize-333858.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[One renter and 175 years of creaking floors: Inside Calista Hill’s unusual new home]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132832708.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Calista Hill recently became the only resident of a beautifully restored eight-unit brownstone, moving in just before others purchased their units. While some social media commentary hinted at ghostly presences, Hill attributed the unexplained sounds to the vintage architecture. Open house viewings are in progress, and soon, new neighbors will join her in this historic building.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/etimes/trending/one-renter-eight-apartments-and-175-years-of-creaking-floors-inside-calista-hills-unusual-new-home/articleshow/132832708.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/etimes/trending/one-renter-eight-apartments-and-175-years-of-creaking-floors-inside-calista-hills-unusual-new-home/articleshow/132832708.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-03T19:06:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Trending Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132832708,imgsize-762361.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Beaten until they enlisted': Russia ramps up forced recruitment amid Ukraine losses - report]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132833134.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/beaten-unt